A||||3||Cheever2||Did I do good?||||5||
Z||000000||Cheever2||07-18-2001||04:28 PM||||I was at work last night, all caught up on Forum reading, looking for someplace else to surf.  Seems my local club's site never has anything new.  Haven't checked eBay in a couple of weeks, and I had a few bucks burning a hole in my Paypal account.  One of the first things I saw was a GT taillight which would end the bidding in 27 minutes!  And it was still affordable at about 50 dollars.  Since the one off my parts car is too scratched to repair, I was thinking of cutting off the clear part and repainting the rest, an idea I got from here... <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=592824984&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=592824984&r=0&t=0</A> <BR>Well, I figured if this eBay one didn't go too high I would try to get it.  Had to bump up my bid twice in the last couple of minutes, finally deciding if it goes over $59 then someone else can have it.  But time ran out at $57.86, so it's mine.  The cool thing is the seller's location is Texas.  I email'd him immediately to say if he's not too far I'd pick it up, but most of Texas is "far" so it was a slim-to-none chance.  He writes back and what do ya know, he's in the north part of Houston.  Even that's up to an hour away, but his son works in the southwest Houston area not far from me, and I will be meeting him to get it.  Small world.<P>And I didn't even see the item in eBay until 27 minutes before the bidding ended.  Just kinda worked out for me this time, huh?<BR><P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator||||reg||5
Z||000001||LT1 Chop Top||07-18-2001||06:35 PM||||Wanna sell them?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||07-18-2001||06:47 PM||||The ones in the link above I did not buy, I just considered doing mine like that as a last resort, cause I'm cheap.  But I have not done it to mine yet.<P>Here's the one I bought last night... <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=593228253&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=593228253&r=0&t=0</A> <P>I'm going to use the back part of the one I have now, and use the lenses & clear cover off the one I just got, and will then have a nice taillight.  My driver's side was not hurt by the wreck I had a long time ago.<P>So, to answer your question, I have no taillights to sell.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||07-18-2001||08:21 PM||||Well Done Cheever.<P>How about I shock you with what fastback tail lights cost here. <P>Hows AU $1000 each sound...ouch hey. OK that was new price but second hand isn't much cheaper.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||||reg||1
